E
"torch torches"
"Wooden torches are spaced fairly evenly, if far apart, on the way up the

stairwell.  Occasionally one sputters on the verge of going out, but then

rekindles with a new flame.  They are set in iron grates which are somehow

bolted into the stone wall.

"
E
