"A Dimly Lit Passage"
"The hall runs off to the east and west with a small wooden door directly to

the south.  The floor, walls, and ceiling are made up of large granite blocks

which seem to be held together simply by the maginitude of their own weight. 

A small glowing orb gives a faint light to this portion of the passage.

