#83212
"A Collapsed Passageway"
"This portion of the granite passageway has been blocked off by a rather

extensive collapse to the north.  Portions of the ceiling and walls have

crumbled in, forming an effective barrier.  A small orb of sickly yellow light

can be seen half buried in the collapse, though it still lights the chamber to

a small degree.  The passage continues to the south.

"
