#83249
"A Small Cell"
"This room is obviously a cell of some sort.  The granite floor, covered in

putrid smelling straw, intermixes with other waste to create a rather unique

olfactory sensation.  The stone walls are spattered with what appear to be

rust colored stains, reflected strangely by the only light coming into the

cell, through the small barred hole in the wooden door to the south.

"
""
301465604 0
0 6 0
D2
""
""
131 -1 83208 0 5
E
"floor straw waste"
"The floor appears to have been used as a battlefield, latrine, and dinner

table, and all at the same time.  In some places, the straw floats in

unidentifiable liquids, unidentifiable for the reason that you don't want to

